# edge_cases C++ bindings

A header-only C++17 wrapper over the `edge_cases` C ABI. `edge_cases.hpp`
includes the C header beside it; every declaration lives in
`namespace edge_cases`.

## Prerequisites

- CMake 3.14 or later
- A C++17 compiler
- The `edge_cases` native library (`libedge_cases.so`, `libedge_cases.dylib`, or
  `edge_cases.dll`)

## Use with CMake

```cmake
add_subdirectory(path/to/cpp)
add_executable(app main.cpp)
target_link_libraries(app PRIVATE edge_cases::cpp)
```

`edge_cases::cpp` adds this directory to the include path, requires
C++17, and links the native library: the file named by the `EDGE_CASES_LIBRARY`
CMake cache variable or environment variable when set, or else
`edge_cases` by name.

```cpp
#include "edge_cases.hpp"
```

The first free function, constructor, or static member you call checks
that the linked library matches these headers and throws
`edge_cases::LoadError` if it doesn't; call `edge_cases::check_library()`
at startup to check eagerly.

